                                   <h1 class="MarginTopTwo TextSizeThreeXL BoldFont TightTracking TextGrayNineHundred SmallBreakpointTextSizeFourXL">Roomcraft Interiors Privacy Policy</h1>
                                   <p class="MarginTopEight">Roomcraft Interiors respects your privacy and is committed to protecting your personal data. This policy explains how we collect, use and protect personal data when you contact us, request a quotation, use our interior design services or interact with our website.</p>
                                   <p class="MarginTopEight">
                                          <strong>Who we are</strong>
                                          Roomcraft Interiors is the controller of the personal data described in this policy. You can contact us using the contact details provided on our website or in your correspondence with us.
                                   </p>
                                   <p class="MarginTopEight">
                                          <strong>Personal data we collect</strong>
                                          Depending on how you interact with us, we may collect your name, contact details, project and property information, communications with us, service preferences, payment and transaction information, and information you choose to provide. When you visit our website, technical information such as your IP address, browser type and information about how you use the site may also be collected through cookies or similar technologies, where applicable.
                                   </p>
                                   <p class="MarginTopEight">
                                          <strong>How we use your data and our legal bases</strong>
                                          We use personal data to respond to enquiries, prepare proposals, provide and manage interior design services, communicate with you, process payments, maintain business records and improve our services. We may also use it to meet legal obligations, protect our rights and prevent or investigate misuse.
                                   </p>
                                   <p class="MarginTopEight">Under UK data protection law, we rely on one or more of these legal bases: taking steps at your request before entering into a contract, performing a contract with you, complying with a legal obligation, pursuing our legitimate interests, or obtaining your consent where required. Our legitimate interests may include operating and improving our business and services. Where we rely on consent, you may withdraw it at any time.</p>
                                   <p class="MarginTopEight">
                                          <strong>Sharing your personal data</strong>
                                          We may share relevant data with service providers who support our business, such as website, IT, payment, accounting or project-related providers, and with professional advisers or public authorities where necessary. We require service providers to protect personal data and use it only for authorised purposes. We do not sell your personal data.
                                   </p>
                                   <p class="MarginTopEight">
                                          <strong>International transfers</strong>
                                          If personal data is transferred outside the UK, we will ensure that appropriate safeguards are in place as required by data protection law.
                                   </p>
                                   <p class="MarginTopEight">
                                          <strong>How long we keep your data</strong>
                                          We keep personal data only for as long as necessary for the purposes described in this policy, including to provide services, manage our business, meet legal and accounting requirements, and resolve disputes. The appropriate period depends on the type of information and why we hold it.
                                   </p>
                                   <p class="MarginTopEight">
                                          <strong>Your rights</strong>
                                          Subject to applicable law, you may have the right to access your personal data, correct inaccurate data, request erasure or restriction of processing, object to certain processing, request data portability, and withdraw consent where processing is based on consent. To exercise a right, contact us using the details provided on our website or in your correspondence with us.
                                   </p>
                                   <p class="MarginTopEight">You may also complain to the UK Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) at ico.org.uk. We would appreciate the opportunity to address your concerns first.</p>
                                   <p class="MarginTopEight">
                                          <strong>Cookies and website technologies</strong>
                                          Our website may use cookies or similar technologies to operate, understand usage or support website features. Where required, we will ask for your consent before using non-essential cookies. You can manage cookies through your browser settings and, where available, our website's cookie controls.
                                   </p>
                                   <p class="MarginTopEight">
                                          <strong>Changes to this policy</strong>
                                          We may update this policy from time to time. The latest version will be published on our website, together with its updated date.
                                   </p>
